# Line endings are LF everywhere, on every platform.
#
# Go's gofmt refuses CRLF and rewrites files on sight, so a `core.autocrlf=true`
# checkout (the Windows default, which is also what the windows-latest runner
# uses) made `gofmt -l .` list the entire tree — a CI failure that says nothing
# about the code. Declaring the normalisation here makes a clone identical in
# content on every machine, which is what `-trimpath` and reproducible builds
# assume anyway.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Never normalise binaries.
*.png binary
*.ico binary
*.syso binary
*.db binary
*.exe binary

# PowerShell scripts keep CRLF: Windows PowerShell 5.1 mis-parses a
# line-continuation backtick at the end of an LF-only line in some hosts, and
# these scripts only ever run on Windows.
*.ps1 text eol=crlf
